    "ym-prove-state-weighted-defect-transfer",
    "Construct, prove, falsify, and audit retained-boundary-state weighted defect-transfer kernels for nonlinear lattice Yang--Mills measures. Use when scalar worst-history conditioning is too strong, rare frustrated states must retain their energetic cost, or local typical-set estimates must be converted into connected-cluster suppression without assuming Bernoulli domination.",
    "---\nname: ym-prove-state-weighted-defect-transfer\ndescription: Construct, prove, falsify, and audit retained-boundary-state weighted defect-transfer kernels for nonlinear lattice Yang--Mills measures. Use when scalar worst-history conditioning is too strong, rare frustrated states must retain their energetic cost, or local typical-set estimates must be converted into connected-cluster suppression without assuming Bernoulli domination.\n---\n\n# Prove State-Weighted Yang--Mills Defect Transfer\n\n## Abducer Integration Guards\n\n- Activate this skill only for `yang-mills-existence-and-mass-gap-target` or an explicitly marked Yang--Mills calibration task.\n- Treat the imported 2026-07-21 portfolio as target-specific incumbent-program evidence, not as plural conceptual discovery and never as a Clay-level result.\n- Require a current target literature rebase before novelty, priority, or investment claims. Preserve the source-to-theory delta and exclusion ledger.\n- Emit claim level, non-claims, hard gate, hypotheses, falsifier, and demotion trigger before promotion.\n- Compose with target-neutral proof-depth, anti-definitionality, same-domain transfer, reflective-conceptual, and declarative-learning controls.\n- Keep symbolic and simulation checks subordinate to the theory-generated kernel inequality; they calibrate or falsify but do not manufacture physical uniformity.\n- Preserve the gauge group, pure-gauge content, observable algebra, regulator, retained-state sufficiency, cutoff/volume quantifiers, reflection positivity, locality, and OS reconstruction route.\n- Source provenance: `agentic/external/yang_mills_representational_dynamics/2026-07-21/active_snapshot/11_vscode_codex_skill_bundle/.agents/skills/ym-prove-state-weighted-defect-transfer/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Exact Target and Version Scope\n\n- Exact target ID: `yang-mills-existence-and-mass-gap-target`.\n- Imported source version: `2026-07-21`, at the source-provenance path above. Treat it as source identity, not evidence that a current frontier search has completed.\n- Authorized theorem scope: finite-regulator retained-state kernels, one-scale weighted defect transfer, and connected-chain bounds with explicit uniform volume, boundary, and cutoff quantifiers.\n- A target-neutral kernel calibration must carry a different target ID and a non-transfer marker. It cannot alter the canonical Yang--Mills claim ledger without a same-theory proof handoff.\n\n## Required Inputs\n\nRequire:\n\n1. Exact target ID, run ID, theorem/proof-obligation ID, current hard gate, and claim ledger.\n2. The newest target-scoped literature snapshot ID and digest, assimilation receipt, and citations for every kernel, drift, or cluster theorem being used. Stale or unresolved literature blocks novelty and priority claims.\n3. Finite regulator, volume, boundary law, cutoff/heat time, block graph and degree `Delta`, exposure order, retained state space, conditional fiber, bad predicate, and next-state map.\n4. A proof of retained-state conditional sufficiency, a positive bad subkernel `Q`, a proposed measurable weight `V>=1`, root-state law, and all constants with their parameter dependence.\n5. Source-artifact paths and digests for finite-matrix optimization, symbolic checks, simulations, mechanized kernels, and hostile cases.\n\n## Theorem Target\n\nFor retained boundary states `sigma`, a positive weight `V>=1`, and a bad extension subkernel `Q`, prove\n\n```text\nintegral V(sigma') Q(sigma,d sigma') <= q_V V(sigma)\n```\n\nwith `exp(alpha) Delta^2 q_V < 1` and a uniform root-state `V` moment. Then derive connected-chain and rooted-cluster decay by positive-kernel iteration.\n\n## Mathematical Invariants\n\nThe mathematical objects are a retained state space `S`, a positive sub-Markov kernel `Q`, a measurable Lyapunov weight `V:S->[1,infinity)`, a root law `mu`, and constants `q_V`, `alpha`, and `Delta`. Preserve:\n\n- The pointwise weighted drift inequality `QV(sigma) <= q_V V(sigma)` for every state in the declared support, with one `q_V` uniform in volume, admissible boundary law, and cutoff range.\n- Kernel positivity: applying `Q` preserves inequalities, so induction gives `Q^nV <= q_V^n V`. No cancellation-based estimate may be substituted for this positive-kernel implication.\n- The initial moment `integral V dmu <= M` is finite with `M` uniform in the declared root states; the weight may not hide an unbounded entry cost.\n- The strict cluster invariant `exp(alpha) Delta^2 q_V < 1` is checked with the same graph and connected-animal convention used in the final sum.\n- Retained-state sufficiency, gauge covariance, locality, reflection compatibility, center, cut-locus/orbit, topology labels, and observable content survive the quotient, transition, and good/charged decomposition.\n- Finite Perron--Frobenius optimization may choose `V` only from the declared kernel. Neither `V` nor `Q` may depend on the desired continuum or spectral-gap conclusion.\n\n## Epistemic Discipline\n\nGive every main claim one status: `conjectural`, `proof-obligation`, `validated-finite`, `blocked`, or `refuted`. Use `validated-finite` only when `Q`, `V`, the drift inequality, and the uniform root moment come from the complete nonlinear conditional measure. A finite matrix, symbolic derivation, simulation, or restricted model is calibration/falsification evidence and cannot manufacture physical uniformity. Cite literature and theorem IDs, artifact paths and digests, or explicit unknowns. Reject circular weights defined from the desired gap, continuum existence, or confinement.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Freeze the finite regulator, volume, block graph, boundary state, fiber, bad predicate, exploration order, and heat-time/cutoff parameters.\n2. Prove the retained state is conditionally sufficient using relative tree gauge or another exact quotient. Preserve boundary gauge covariance, reflection compatibility, center, cut-locus, orbit, and topology data.\n3. Prove `QV<=q_V V => Q^nV<=q_V^nV` and include the initial `V` moment.\n4. Optimize finite multitype weights by Perron--Frobenius analysis. Permit a large scalar conditional only when the weight proves its entry cost independently.\n5. Define the good region with local link, plaquette-input, or curvature norms.\n6. Prove normalized good-channel comparison with partition functions, Haar/Jacobian factors, chart overlap, and boundary dependence.\n7. Prove multi-link weighted energy charging for center, continuous, cut-locus/orbit, and topological complement channels.\n8. Combine kernels, verify the strict threshold, test hostile histories, and finish with a theorem graph and frontier ledger.\n\n## Mandatory Falsifications\n\n- Test `Q=[[0,q^2],[1,0]]` with weight `[1,1/q]`.\n- Retain the anticorrelated two-site moment counterexample.\n- Test negative-center boundaries and continuous incoherent collars.\n- Compare local concentration with every proposed global-ball certificate.\n- Reject nonpositive weights, invalid kernels, critical thresholds, hidden volume factors, and weights defined using the desired gap.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn a machine-reviewable packet containing:\n\n- target, run, source-version, literature-snapshot, theorem, and obligation IDs with evidence citations and source-artifact digests;\n- typed state/fiber disintegration, positive-mass support, proof of retained-state sufficiency, weight, root law, and bad subkernel;\n- good-channel and charged-complement inequalities, the pointwise drift proof, iterated bound, uniform root moment, strict threshold, and cluster sum;\n- finite Perron--Frobenius or other optimization artifacts separated from the analytic uniformity proof;\n- counterexamples and hostile-state results, parameter-dependence ledger, dependency graph, epistemic status per edge, explicit unknowns, non-claims, and first open implication.\n\nNever promote a finite overlap window to RG, continuum, OS, or Hamiltonian-gap control.\n\n## Failure/Demotion\n\nDemote to `blocked` when retained states are not sufficient, `Q` is not positive/sub-Markov on the declared support, `V` is nonpositive or has an unbounded root moment, uniformity is missing, or the strict threshold fails. Mark the formulation `refuted` when an admissible retained state violates the weighted drift inequality or a hostile example defeats the proposed sufficiency/iteration. Quarantine weights that encode the desired answer, stale-literature novelty claims, hidden volume factors, and computational evidence presented as an analytic theorem. Preserve failed root moments and hostile states as reusable negative knowledge.\n\n## Validation Handoff\n\nRun `python agentic/scripts/validate_ym_representational_dynamics_20260721.py --allow-open-todos` and `python -m pytest -q tests/domains/test_ym_representational_dynamics_20260721.py`. Then send frontier/source claims to `ym-audit-frontier` and proof status to `proof-depth-release-gate`. The deterministic validators verify integration and evidence contracts, not theorem truth; any open drift, root-moment, or sufficiency obligation returns to the reflective parent cycle.\n\n## Packaged PRISM Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly the generated `ConditionalDerivationPacket` JSON object. Do not paraphrase closed variant values.\n\n- Follow the exact generated JSON schema without extra fields.\n",
